From ea657fdecf6e588313532d7b9bfec873d2f318c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:45:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/59] Switch Vulkan: cheaper explosions - RGBA8 scene, sprite
 alpha cut, draw-based upscale

Console logs (4cd05c98b): outside explosions the game holds 60 fps; in
Brutal Doom explosions 400-650 sprites (200-430 translucent) make frames of
100-200 ms that are GPU time even at 60% resolution. Sprites are lit per
sprite on the CPU, so the cost is blending: hundreds of smoke layers over
the view.

- The scene is RGBA8 by default (rd_vk_scenefmt 2): with bloom and
  tonemapping off the image is the same, and blending runs at full rate
  with half the traffic of RGBA16F.
- Translucent sprite fragments below rd_sprite_alphacut (0.02) are
  discarded instead of blended.
- The dynamic resolution stretches the view with a textured draw
  (shaders/pp/upscale.fp) instead of vkCmdBlitImage, which cost 2-4 ms per
  frame on NVK; the controller models the frame at full scale and climbs
  back as soon as the predicted frame fits (it stayed at 60% for the whole
  session after the first explosion).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
